## Architectural Decisions

- Project working memory should use a lightweight three-layer scheme: daily notes in `memory/YYYY-MM-DD.md`, recurring topic notes in `memory/topic-<slug>.md`, and durable distilled project memory in `assistant-memory.md`.
- Daily files should stay short and point to topic files when discussions become recurring, architecturally meaningful, or too long for a brief chronological note.
- The project memory scheme should remain compatible with the shared cross-project convention from `{{GLOBAL_MEMORY_DIR}}/memory-architecture.md`: global rules in the global memory directory, durable project rules in `assistant-memory.md`, and project working context in `memory/`.

## Project Process Agreements

- After each logically completed project step, update the relevant project context files before considering the step finished.
- Keep one source of truth per information type; prefer links over duplicate text.
